%N A181381 Total number of positive integers below 10^n requiring 5 positive cubes in their representation as sum of cubes.
%C A181381 A061439(n) + A181375(n) + A181377(n) + A181379(n) + a(n) + A181400(n) + A181402(n) + A181404(n) + A130130(n) = A002283(n)
%C A181381 Deshouillers et al. (2000) conjectured that there are exactly 113936676 positive integers which are not the sum of four nonnegative integral cubes, and that the largest is 7373170279850. Combined with earlier proofs and conjectures, this would imply a(n) = 113932616 for n >= 13. - _Martin Fuller_, Oct 11 2026
